[110.3, "o", "\r\nHere is a summary of the Phase 3 adversarial code review.\r\n\r\n**Findings written to:** `/Users/jonr/Documents/non-nitro-repos/timbre/docs/holtz/audit/3-adversarial.md`\r\n**Punchlist appended:** `/Users/jonr/Documents/non-nitro-repos/timbre/docs/holtz/PUNCHLIST.md` (BH-200 through BH-215)\r\n**Status updated:** `/Users/jonr/Documents/non-nitro-repos/timbre/docs/holtz/STATUS.md`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**16 findings total: 2 HIGH, 6 MEDIUM, 8 LOW**\r\n\r\n**The two HIGH-severity findings share a root cause and should be fixed together:**\r\n\r\n- **BH-200 + BH-214** -- `AccessibilityClampPass` uses 2 luminance readback buffers but the render loop allows 3 frames in flight. The CPU reads from (and zeros) a `.shared` MTLBuffer that the GPU may still be writing to. This is a data race on the safety-critical flash rate limiter that enforces WCAG 2.3.1 seizure prevention. Fix: increase buffer count to 3 to match the inflight semaphore, or add GPU fence synchronization.\r\n\r\n**Key MEDIUM findings:**\r\n\r\n- **BH-201** -- `stop()` does not cancel the analysis drain loop (latent double-start bug)\r\n- **BH-202** -- No orchestrator teardown on window close (resource leak, future screensaver concern)\r\n- **BH-203** -- Weak delegate nil-check on real-time audio thread reintroduces the ARC ops the Unmanaged pattern was designed to avoid\r\n- **BH-205** -- Partially-encoded command buffers committed when blit/compositor encoder creation fails\r\n- **BH-206** -- PingPongFramebuffer and BloomPass never resized on window resize (confirmed TODO RK-2)\r\n- **BH-209** -- Deferred bootstrap proceeds with 1x1 framebuffer if retries exhausted, no error shown\r\n\r\nNo source code was modified. All findings are documented in the audit and punchlist files.\r\n"]
