[229.9, "o", "\u001b[2m  [248,278 ctx | 4 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[230.7, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Read\u001b[0m \u001b[2mjustine/SUMMARY.md\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[230.85, "o", "\r\nJustine's findings align with mine. Her key patterns (GPU Rubber Stamp, Tested-But-Unwired, Missing Resize) are all addressed or captured in the punchlist. Let me present the results.\r\n"]
[232.35, "o", "\u001b[2m  [250,492 ctx | 11 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[233.15, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Write\u001b[0m \u001b[2mholtz/STATUS.md\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[233.3, "o", "\r\nHere's what was accomplished:\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\n\r\n### Primary Deliverable: Programmatic Validation\r\n**`FullPipelineIntegrationTests.swift`** \u2014 6 tests that prove the app displays correctly without a human in the loop:\r\n\r\n| Test | What it proves |\r\n|------|---------------|\r\n| `testFullPipelineProducesNonBlackOutput` | Audio \u2192 DSP \u2192 TripleBuffer \u2192 RenderPipeline \u2192 non-black pixels |\r\n| `testRenderedOutputDiffersBetweenSignalAndSilence` | Audio signal produces more visible output than silence |\r\n| `testTripleBufferCarriesAudioFeatures` | DSP-computed AudioFeatureFrame survives TripleBuffer write/read |\r\n| `testMultipleFramesRenderStably` | 30 frames render without crash or NaN propagation |\r\n| `testSilenceToSignalTransition` | Transition from silence to signal produces visible output |\r\n| `testPostProcessingChainIsActive` | Bloom + CA + film grain modify the output |\r\n\r\n### Bonus: Runtime Metal Shader Compilation\r\n**`PipelineBootstrap.compileFromBundledSources`** \u2014 When SPM bundles `.metal` files as source (debug builds), this method concatenates and compiles them at runtime. This enabled 5 GPU tests to pass via `swift test` that previously skipped.\r\n\r\n**Test metrics:** 624 \u2192 **630 passing** (0 failing, 115 skipping)\r\n\r\n### Audit Findings: 30 items across 3 phases\r\n- **7 HIGH** (3 test/integration-gap, 2 bug/concurrency, 2 test quality)\r\n- **11 MEDIUM** (lifecycle, error handling, test quality)\r\n- **12 LOW** (documentation, minor code quality)\r\n\r\n**Top remaining items by priority:**\r\n1. **BH-200/BH-214** (HIGH): AccessibilityClampPass uses 2 readback buffers with 3 inflight frames \u2014 safety-critical data race\r\n2. **BH-201** (MEDIUM): `stop()` doesn't halt the analysis drain loop\r\n3. **BH-206** (MEDIUM): PingPongFramebuffer never resized on window resize\r\n\r\nAll findings are in `docs/holtz/PUNCHLIST.md`. Full audit data in `docs/holtz/`.\r\n"]
[234.8, "o", "\u001b[2m  [251,515 ctx | 561 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[235.6, "o", "\r\nAll background agents have reported in. The audit and fix work is complete. Here's where things stand:\r\n\r\n**Delivered:**\r\n- 6 new integration tests proving audio \u2192 rendering \u2192 pixels works (`swift test --filter FullPipelineIntegrationTests`)\r\n- Runtime Metal shader compilation enabling GPU tests in SPM context\r\n- 630 passing / 0 failing / 115 skipping (up from 624 passing)\r\n- Full audit with 30 punchlist items in `docs/holtz/PUNCHLIST.md`\r\n\r\n**Remaining HIGH items** if you want me to continue into the punchlist:\r\n1. **BH-200/214** \u2014 AccessibilityClampPass double-buffer race (safety-critical, shared root cause)\r\n2. **BH-104** \u2014 RenderCoordinator only has 3 tests\r\n\r\nLet me know if you'd like me to keep working through the punchlist or if you want to review what's here first.\r\n"]
[237.1, "o", "\u001b[2m  [258,545 ctx | 222 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[237.9, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[35m\u276f commit as you go, and keep working through the punchlist\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[239.9, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Bash\u001b[0m \u001b[2mShow working tree status\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[240.05, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Bash\u001b[0m \u001b[2mShow diff summary\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[240.2, "o", "  \u001b[2m  ... +1 more tool calls ...\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[240.35, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Bash\u001b[0m \u001b[2mCommit integration tests and shader compilation\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[240.5, "o", "\r\nGood, committed. Now tackling **BH-200/BH-214** \u2014 the AccessibilityClampPass double-buffer race. This is safety-critical.\r\n"]
[242.0, "o", "\u001b[2m  [260,297 ctx | 1 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[242.8, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Read\u001b[0m \u001b[2mRendering/AccessibilityClampPass.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[242.95, "o", "\r\nThe race is clear: 2 readback buffers with 3 inflight frames means Frame 2 can zero buffer[0] while Frame 0's GPU is still writing to it. Fix: 3 buffers to match inflight count.\r\n"]
[244.45, "o", "\u001b[2m  [267,727 ctx | 9 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[245.25, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Edit\u001b[0m \u001b[2mRendering/AccessibilityClampPass.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[245.4, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Edit\u001b[0m \u001b[2mRendering/AccessibilityClampPass.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[245.55, "o", "\r\nNow update the buffer index calculations from `% 2` to `% 3`:\r\n"]
[247.05, "o", "\u001b[2m  [270,286 ctx | 1 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[247.85, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Edit\u001b[0m \u001b[2mRendering/AccessibilityClampPass.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[248.0, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Edit\u001b[0m \u001b[2mRendering/AccessibilityClampPass.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[248.15, "o", "\r\nNow run the tests to verify nothing broke:\r\n"]
[249.65, "o", "\u001b[2m  [270,771 ctx | 1 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[250.45, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Bash\u001b[0m \u001b[2mRun accessibility and integration tests\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[250.6, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Bash\u001b[0m \u001b[2mCount passing tests\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[250.75, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Bash\u001b[0m \u001b[2mCount failures\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[250.9, "o", "\r\nAll pass. Let me commit this fix and move to the next item.\r\n"]
[252.4, "o", "\u001b[2m  [272,303 ctx | 1 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[253.2, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Bash\u001b[0m \u001b[2mCommit AccessibilityClampPass fix\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[253.35, "o", "\r\nNext: **BH-201** \u2014 `stop()` doesn't halt the analysis drain loop. This is a real lifecycle bug.\r\n"]
[254.85, "o", "\u001b[2m  [272,697 ctx | 1 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[255.65, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Read\u001b[0m \u001b[2mApp/TimbreOrchestrator.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[255.8, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Edit\u001b[0m \u001b[2mApp/TimbreOrchestrator.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[255.95, "o", "\r\nNow add a stopped flag to the class:\r\n"]
[257.45, "o", "\u001b[2m  [274,483 ctx | 1 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[258.25, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Edit\u001b[0m \u001b[2mApp/TimbreOrchestrator.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[258.4, "o", "\r\nNow update `stop()` to set the flag:\r\n"]
[259.9, "o", "\u001b[2m  [274,821 ctx | 1 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[260.7, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Edit\u001b[0m \u001b[2mApp/TimbreOrchestrator.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[260.85, "o", "\r\nNow update `scheduleAnalysisDrain` to check the stopped flag:\r\n"]
[262.35, "o", "\u001b[2m  [275,149 ctx | 3 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[263.15, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Edit\u001b[0m \u001b[2mApp/TimbreOrchestrator.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[263.3, "o", "\r\nAlso reset the stopped flag in `start()` to prevent issues if start is called after stop:\r\n"]
[264.8, "o", "\u001b[2m  [275,667 ctx | 1 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[265.6, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Edit\u001b[0m \u001b[2mApp/TimbreOrchestrator.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[265.75, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Bash\u001b[0m \u001b[2mVerify build\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[265.9, "o", "  \u001b[2m  ... +1 more tool calls ...\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[266.05, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Bash\u001b[0m \u001b[2mCommit analysis drain loop fix\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[266.2, "o", "\r\nNext: **BH-211** \u2014 CA/FilmGrain init not wrapped in do/catch (asymmetric error handling). Quick fix.\r\n"]
[267.7, "o", "\u001b[2m  [277,051 ctx | 1 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[268.5, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Read\u001b[0m \u001b[2mApp/TimbreOrchestrator.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[268.65, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Grep\u001b[0m \u001b[2m/public init\\(device.*pipelineCache\"/\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[268.8, "o", "  \u001b[2m  ... +7 more tool calls ...\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[268.95, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Read\u001b[0m \u001b[2mRendering/ChromaticAberrationPass.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[269.1, "o", "\r\nThe init is non-throwing, but `pipelineCache.renderPipeline(forKey:)` will crash with a precondition failure if the key is missing. The issue is that it uses a force-unwrap style API (precondition) rather than throwing. The fix in BH-211 is to make the orchestrator's usage consistent with BloomPass \u2014 use do/catch. But since the CA/FilmGrain inits don't throw, I need to either make them throw or just accept the asymmetry.\r\n\r\nThe real concern from BH-211 is that if the pipeline key is ever missing, Bloom degrades gracefully but CA/FilmGrain crash. Let me make these optional like Bloom:\r\n"]
[270.6, "o", "\u001b[2m  [279,445 ctx | 1 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[271.4, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Edit\u001b[0m \u001b[2mApp/TimbreOrchestrator.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[271.55, "o", "\r\nNow I need to check if PipelineCache has a `hasRenderPipeline` method:\r\n"]
[273.05, "o", "\u001b[2m  [280,120 ctx | 5 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[273.85, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Grep\u001b[0m \u001b[2m/func.*renderPipeline|func.*has\"/\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[274.0, "o", "\r\nNo `has` method. Let me check the renderPipeline method:\r\n"]
[275.5, "o", "\u001b[2m  [280,293 ctx | 1 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[276.3, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Read\u001b[0m \u001b[2mRendering/PipelineCache.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[276.45, "o", "\r\nIt `fatalError`s. Let me add a `hasRenderPipeline` check method:\r\n"]
[277.95, "o", "\u001b[2m  [280,708 ctx | 1 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[278.75, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Edit\u001b[0m \u001b[2mRendering/PipelineCache.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[278.9, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Bash\u001b[0m \u001b[2mVerify build\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[279.05, "o", "  \u001b[2m  ... +1 more tool calls ...\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[279.2, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Bash\u001b[0m \u001b[2mCommit defensive post-processing init\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[279.35, "o", "\r\nNext: **BH-205** \u2014 Silent frame degradation on encoder failure. The render pipeline silently commits partially-encoded command buffers when blit/compositor encoder creation fails.\r\n"]
[280.85, "o", "\u001b[2m  [281,886 ctx | 1 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[281.65, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Read\u001b[0m \u001b[2mRendering/RenderPipeline.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[281.8, "o", "\r\nThe issue is in `encodeBlitPass` and `encodeCompositorPass` \u2014 they silently `return` on encoder failure. Let me make them return a success Bool so `renderFrame` can abort:\r\n"]
[283.3, "o", "\u001b[2m  [282,530 ctx | 1 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[284.1, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Read\u001b[0m \u001b[2mRendering/RenderPipeline.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[284.25, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Edit\u001b[0m \u001b[2mRendering/RenderPipeline.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[284.4, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Edit\u001b[0m \u001b[2mRendering/RenderPipeline.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[284.55, "o", "\r\nNow update `renderFrame` to abort on blit/compositor failure (the critical intermediate\u2192drawable blit):\r\n"]
[286.05, "o", "\u001b[2m  [285,147 ctx | 1 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[286.85, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Read\u001b[0m \u001b[2mRendering/RenderPipeline.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[287.0, "o", "\r\nNow update the final P3 blit to abort on failure:\r\n"]
[288.5, "o", "\u001b[2m  [285,624 ctx | 1 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[289.3, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Read\u001b[0m \u001b[2mRendering/RenderPipeline.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[289.45, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Edit\u001b[0m \u001b[2mRendering/RenderPipeline.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[289.6, "o", "  \u001b[2m  ... +2 more tool calls ...\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[289.75, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Bash\u001b[0m \u001b[2mCommit encoder failure handling\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[289.9, "o", "\r\nNext: **BH-206** \u2014 PingPongFramebuffer never resized on window resize. Let me wire the resize call.\r\n"]
[291.4, "o", "\u001b[2m  [287,199 ctx | 1 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[292.2, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Grep\u001b[0m \u001b[2m/func resize|func drawableSize\"/\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[292.35, "o", "\r\nGood, `resize()` exists. Now I need to detect drawable size changes in the render loop and call resize. The best place is in `RenderPipeline.renderFrame()` \u2014 it already gets the drawable texture and calls `ensureCompositorTexture`.\r\n"]
[293.85, "o", "\u001b[2m  [287,553 ctx | 1 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[294.65, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Read\u001b[0m \u001b[2mRendering/RenderPipeline.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[294.8, "o", "\r\nI need to track the last known drawable size and resize when it changes. Let me add this to RenderPipeline:\r\n"]
[296.3, "o", "\u001b[2m  [288,276 ctx | 1 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[297.1, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Edit\u001b[0m \u001b[2mRendering/RenderPipeline.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[297.25, "o", "\r\nNow add resize detection after acquiring the drawable:\r\n"]
[298.75, "o", "\u001b[2m  [288,593 ctx | 2 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[299.55, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Edit\u001b[0m \u001b[2mRendering/RenderPipeline.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[299.7, "o", "\r\nNow check if BloomPass has a resize method:\r\n"]
[301.2, "o", "\u001b[2m  [289,188 ctx | 2 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[302.0, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Grep\u001b[0m \u001b[2m/func resize\"/\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[302.15, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Grep\u001b[0m \u001b[2m/resize\"/\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[302.3, "o", "\r\nBloomPass has no resize method. Let me remove that call and just note it as a known limitation:\r\n"]
[303.8, "o", "\u001b[2m  [289,435 ctx | 1 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[304.6, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Edit\u001b[0m \u001b[2mRendering/RenderPipeline.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[304.75, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Bash\u001b[0m \u001b[2mVerify tests still pass\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[304.9, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Bash\u001b[0m \u001b[2mCommit framebuffer resize fix\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[305.05, "o", "\r\nNext: **BH-202** \u2014 No orchestrator teardown on window close. Let me add a `scenePhase` observer:\r\n"]
[306.55, "o", "\u001b[2m  [290,781 ctx | 1 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[307.35, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Read\u001b[0m \u001b[2mTimbreApp/TimbreAppMain.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[307.5, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Edit\u001b[0m \u001b[2mTimbreApp/TimbreAppMain.swift\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[307.65, "o", "  \u001b[2m  ... +1 more tool calls ...\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[307.8, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Bash\u001b[0m \u001b[2mCommit lifecycle teardown\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[307.95, "o", "\r\nNow let me run the full test suite to confirm everything is still green, then continue with more items:\r\n"]
[309.45, "o", "\u001b[2m  [292,131 ctx | 3 out]\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[310.25, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Bash\u001b[0m \u001b[2mCount passing tests\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[310.4, "o", "  \u001b[36m\u23bf Bash\u001b[0m \u001b[2mCount failing tests\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[310.55, "o", "\r\n631 pass, 0 fail. Next: **BH-203** \u2014 Weak delegate check on real-time audio thread. Let me look at MicrophoneCapture:\r\n"]
